{"name":"Madagascar","hex":"#9d8544","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Madagascar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An island and country off the east coast of Africa. Official name: Republic of Madagascar. Capital: Antananarivo."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A resident of Madagascar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Madagascar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Madagascar","blocks":[{"text":"Madagascar, officially the Republic of Madagascar, is an island country in the Indian Ocean that includes the island of Madagascar and numerous smaller peripheral islands. Lying off the southeastern coast of Africa, it is the world's fourth-largest island, the second-largest island country, and the 46th-largest country overall. Its capital and largest city is Antananarivo."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Madagascar_%28centered_orthographic_projection%29.svg/330px-Madagascar_%28centered_orthographic_projection%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madagascar","wikidata":"Q1019"},{"title":"Madagascar (franchise)","blocks":[{"text":"Madagascar is an American media franchise of DreamWorks Animation. The voices of Ben Stiller, Chris Rock, David Schwimmer and Jada Pinkett Smith are featured in the films. It began in 2005 with the release of the animated feature film of the same name, followed by Madagascar: Escape 2 Africa in 2008 and Madagascar 3: Europe's Most Wanted in 2012. A spin-off film featuring the penguins, titled Penguins of Madagascar, was released in 2014. A fourth main film, Madagascar 4, was announced for 2018, but has since been removed from its schedule indefinitely due to the studio's restructuring in 2015."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Madagascar_logo.png/330px-Madagascar_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madagascar_(franchise)","wikidata":"Q2261392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Malagasy_girls_Madagascar_Merina.jpg/500px-Malagasy_girls_Madagascar_Merina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Malagasy_girls_Madagascar_Merina.jpg/1280px-Malagasy_girls_Madagascar_Merina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Malagasy_girls_Madagascar_Merina.jpg/500px-Malagasy_girls_Madagascar_Merina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Malagasy ancestry reflects a blend of Southeast Asian, Oceanian, and Bantu (Southeast African) roots. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMalagasy_girls_Madagascar_Merina.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Andrianampoinimerina_HQ.jpg/500px-Andrianampoinimerina_HQ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Andrianampoinimerina_HQ.jpg/500px-Andrianampoinimerina_HQ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"King Andrianampoinimerina (1787–1810)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAndrianampoinimerina_HQ.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/LaGuerreAMadagascar.jpg/500px-LaGuerreAMadagascar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/LaGuerreAMadagascar.jpg/1280px-LaGuerreAMadagascar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/LaGuerreAMadagascar.jpg/500px-LaGuerreAMadagascar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm